>> Not sure why its doing that.
>
> The parts of the grid external to the dungeon aren't
> "left blank", they are drawn with the "rock" (solid
> black) tile. Probably in scaling, if you did it the
> usual "cubic" way, you interpolated in some color
> of the surrounding tiles, and that tile is no longer
> solid black.
>
> You can:
>
> 1) Find and fix the individual tile.
>
> or
>
> 2) Re-do the scaling in "no interpolation" mode so
>   that you exactly turn each pixel into four pixels
>   with no color blending across original pixel
>   boundaries.
>
>   You probably want to choose this option, because
>   you'll eventually notice similar artifacts in
>   _all_ the tiles, they just don't jump off the
>   screen at you the way mistakes in "solid black"
>   do.
>
